From dcb2be22f9c3776d57e64d5fd7e57f50f79823fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 22:49:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rednsd: the shipped seed of public DoH resolver addresses

The built-in addresses "Block encrypted DNS that goes around the router" uses before
the maintained list has downloaded (and with it): the published anycast addresses of
the large public DNS-over-HTTPS resolvers, /24 at the widest. Public infrastructure,
one per line; encdns.sh validates it like the downloaded list.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/rednsd/doh-seed.txt | 89 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 89 insertions(+)
 create mode 100755 release/src/router/rednsd/doh-seed.txt

diff --git a/release/src/router/rednsd/doh-seed.txt b/release/src/router/rednsd/doh-seed.txt
new file mode 100755
index 00000000000..5bfe80c87a3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/release/src/router/rednsd/doh-seed.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,89 @@
